  "body": "## What changed\n\nA failed window read-back now answers the report request. The status says:\n\n> Screenshot: picture was not copied - the text report is complete\n\nThe completion channel retains the tokens on map, mapped-range and decoding failures. The frame consumes failures before it draws the status strip. A failed picture never produces a screenshot event or a clipboard image. A foreign token does not change the report status.\n\nThe capture remains busy until the frame consumes its result. This keeps the final repaint after the callback clears its flag. Each shot owns its flag, so an obsolete callback after a timeout cannot release or answer a newer shot. Requests that arrived during a failed shot remain queued.\n\nThe change is limited to the native report capture, the frame call, five regression tests and the decision note. It adds no dependency or persistent fault-injection option.\n\n## Reproduction and readings\n\nOn `a7afb5766b5d37073eb075ecda84c3ba70430653`, a cancelled read-back leaves the status at “is copying the window to the clipboard”. The new status assertion fails on that source. It passes with this change.\n\nThe test cancels a real pending wgpu map with `Buffer::unmap`. Linux uses the Vulkan llvmpipe software adapter. This exercises the production map-error callback. It does **not** simulate physical device loss. A separate deterministic test uses the shared callback completion helper and checks the visible status and absence of an image copy.\n\n## Checks\n\nOn source head `e086568649de35370209c8067ca2fdb8834979a6`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: all 10 steps pass. This includes the UI library, the five new capture tests, the existing report tests and eight mapped UI suites.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --only 'motion light:' --only 'app light:'`: all 11 light twins pass in five steps.\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\n- `graphify update .`: completed; generated graph files are not committed.\n\nThe first unrestricted light command reached the foreground time limit during its broad release prebuild. No process remained. The precise command above compiled and ran every discovered light target successfully. The prebuild timeout is not reported as a passed step.\n\nThe regression tests cover:\n\n- failed completion to visible status, without an image copy;\n- cancellation through the real map callback;\n- foreign tokens and a closed report dialog;\n- successful delivery to multiple tokens and a queued request after failure;\n- timeouts and late failure/success replies during a fresh shot.\n\nNo machining, G-code, post, geometry, collision or stock simulation behavior changes. No full heavy lane, GPU parity, example catalog or release package was run. A real lost device was not tested. No required CI rules were returned by the authenticated main rules and ruleset APIs; this is not a green-CI claim.\n\n## Before and after\n\nThese are genuine Linux renders from a temporary test harness. It presses the real report button, cancels the native capture map, consumes the result and draws the production report/status components. It removes the harness's automatic screenshot reply so only the native callback can answer. The harness is not part of this PR. No source or snapshot PNG is included.\n\nBefore, production source `a7afb5766b5d37073eb075ecda84c3ba70430653`:\n\n![Before: status still promises a picture after a failed read-back](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e3c6e67a4ef24977f3b7a2027fe09ce6f0fd03db/before.png)\n\nAfter, production source of `e086568649de35370209c8067ca2fdb8834979a6`:\n\n![After: picture was not copied and text report is complete](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/e3c6e67a4ef24977f3b7a2027fe09ce6f0fd03db/after.png)\n\nThe images are stored on the fork's separate images-only branch.\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/2745#issuecomment-7211092129\n\nChangelog: Report a failed window picture read-back without leaving the status at copying; preserve the complete text report.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2745\n",
